From 90fdf4781879541eec7ae9c197e9ef272d837fe5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:36:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/54] runtime: rest an app's controller hand on the touch
 sensors; quit the app when the headset leaves

A hand holding a tracked controller no longer reports articulated joints:
the client sends joint positions only, so every bone rotation was
invented, and a skeleton built from them (OpenComposite) lost the thumb
and index finger. The app falls back to its controller hand.

That hand is posed from touch: under profiles without the Frame's own
inputs, trigger/touch, thumbstick/touch, thumbrest/touch and the face
buttons' touch now read the client's touch sensors, and a finger resting
on the grip sensor reads as a 0.3 curl on squeeze/value, below the 0.5
click.

exit_app_after_client_gone_s (default 0, off): with no headset client
for that long the session goes LOSS_PENDING, which asks the app to
quit. Quitting a streamed game from the headset menu ended only the
client, and the game played on.
---
